Hi all,

I am using INLA-SPDE approach now and becoming interested in how to implement this approach with inla. I read some R codes like inla.spde2.matern, inla.spde.make.A , etc and searched in the discussion group for a while, but got little about this.

1. I am not very clear about the intuitive meaning of the parameter \nu or \alpha. They relate to the differential operator in the SPDE, do they have any relationship with the smoothness of the solution x(u) to the SPDE?
2. In the codes for the main interface functions such as inla.spde2.matern.., I did not find the procedure for calculating precision matrix using finite element method as in Lindgren et. al (2011). Does the resulted model 'spde=inla.spde2.matern(***)'  " tell " inla how to calculate the precision matrix?
3. In Lindgren et al 2011, a finite element representation with piecewise linear bases is used for approximating the solution x(u) to the SPDE, can we use other bases there? If we can, which part of the codes need to be changed (going back to question 2.) ?

Thanks a lot!

Cheers,
David

